From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mydist <mydist@local>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] proto-ext: acknowledge link-down while tearing down

A link-down notification that arrives while the proto state machine is
already in S_TEARDOWN/S_SETUP_ABORT has nothing left to act on: the
interface is going away and netifd itself asked for the teardown.

proto-shell builds on proto-ext, so the DHCP client script's deconfig
path (proto_init_update "*" 0 in /lib/netifd/dhcp.script) sends exactly
this notification when netifd SIGTERMs udhcpc after a carrier loss.
netifd answered UBUS_STATUS_PERMISSION_DENIED, which the ubus CLI printed
as

  Command failed: ubus call network.interface notify_proto
    { "action": 0, "link-up": false, ... } (Permission denied)

on every link flap. That is not an ACL problem and the deconfig itself
did succeed; the line only made an expected teardown look like a failure
(measured on the lab VM: e1000 carrier bounce at 118 s, one such line,
first lease released and reacquired 3 s later).

Acknowledge a link-down in the teardown states instead. Every other
notification keeps the old "refuse updates while tearing down" answer.

Signed-off-by: mydist <mydist@local>
---
 proto-ext.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/proto-ext.c
+++ b/proto-ext.c
@@ -353,8 +353,25 @@ proto_ext_update_link(struct proto_ext_state *state, struct blob_attr *data, struct blob_attr **tb)
 	bool keep = false;
 	bool up;
 
+	/* A link-down notification that arrives while the proto is already
+	 * being torn down is a no-op, not an error: the interface is going
+	 * away and there is nothing left to update. The DHCP client script
+	 * sends exactly this from its deconfig path when netifd SIGTERMs
+	 * udhcpc after a carrier loss; answering "Permission denied" made
+	 * ubus print
+	 *
+	 *   Command failed: ubus call ... notify_proto (...) (Permission denied)
+	 *
+	 * on every link flap and made an expected teardown look like a
+	 * failure. Acknowledge it instead; all other notifications are still
+	 * refused while the proto is tearing down.
+	 */
+	if ((state->sm == S_TEARDOWN || state->sm == S_SETUP_ABORT) &&
+	    tb[NOTIFY_LINK_UP] && !blobmsg_get_bool(tb[NOTIFY_LINK_UP]))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (state->sm == S_TEARDOWN || state->sm == S_SETUP_ABORT)
 		return UBUS_STATUS_PERMISSION_DENIED;
 
 	if (!tb[NOTIFY_LINK_UP])
 		return UBUS_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT;
